<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25648" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαπρύσιος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>going through, piercing,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only as Adv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὼν
				πεδίοιο διαπρύσιον τετυχηκώς</span> a hill <i>piercing
				into, running out into,</i> the plain, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.748
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of sound,
				<i>piercing, thrilling,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤϋσεν δὲ διαπρύσιον</span> he gave a
				<i>piercing</i> cry, <i><span class="en">
				8.227
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. κιθαρίζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ven.</u>
					80
				</span></i>
			: in late Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τορόν τι βοῶν καὶ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Agath.
					4.11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later as
				Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ʼΑπείρῳ διαπρυσία</span>”
				<i>far-stretching,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					4.51
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> freq. of
			sound, <i>piercing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλολυγαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ven.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄτοβος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					1479
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλαδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1308
				</span></i>
			(lyr.): in late Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰμωγαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					2.1.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. κεραϊστής</span> a <i>downright</i>
			thief, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				336
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. πόλεμος</span>
			<i>open</i> war, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				2.143
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			Adv.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span>
			<i>loudly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστορίας μαρτυρία κηρύττουσα δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					11.38
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <i>intensely,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μισεῖσθαι ὑπό τινος</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				481
			</span></i>.</div>
